Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: user32: Above 96 DPI pick and scale icons like Windows when the size is missing.
 Without an entry of the requested size, the nearest one is used (on a
 tie the first in the file) and resized by pixel replication. At 120 and
 144 DPI that shrinks 48 and 32 pixel icons with dropped rows and enlarges
 16 pixel ones blockily. Above 96 DPI prefer the smallest larger entry,
 enlarge only when there is none, and resample color icons with a filter
 on premultiplied pixels; transparency from the AND mask or alpha channel
 goes into the alpha bitmap and a mask derived from it. Exact sizes, and
 everything at 96 DPI, take the existing path.
